# Mosquitto ACL — mqtt.offx1.com (authoritative, 2026-11-07)
# John confirmed this ACL was applied to the broker on 2026-11-07.
# It adds the watcher write grant for watcher/audio so the console
# page can publish audio directly to the bridge instead of batching
# audio chunks into watcher/telemetry.

# ============ muse user (bridge subscriber + Muse agent) ============
user muse
# Bridge reads page telemetry, status, audio
topic read watcher/telemetry
topic read watcher/status
topic read watcher/audio
# Bridge publishes status here; also receives console pings
topic readwrite watcher/bridge
# Muse agent sends device commands (bridge does not need to read these)
topic write watcher/command
# Keepalive: page publishes config on watcher/keepalive (single writer);
# bridge publishes its own takeover claims on watcher/keepalive_bridge
# (single writer). Daemon subscribes to both; page config wins ties.
topic read watcher/keepalive
topic write watcher/keepalive_bridge
# Jiggler: page publishes pill state on watcher/jiggle (single writer);
# bridge remote-control publishes on watcher/jiggle_bridge (single
# writer). Page applies bridge messages to its jiggler.
topic read watcher/jiggle
topic write watcher/jiggle_bridge
# Muse driving state: agent publishes, bridge monitors
topic readwrite watcher/muse
# Pause state: bidirectional (page publishes pill clicks, agent publishes remote pause)
topic readwrite watcher/muse_pause
# Command queue: bidirectional (page publishes depth, agent can clear)
topic readwrite watcher/muse_queue
# Heartbeats: bridge listens (added 2026-09-25; no consumer in subscriber.py yet)
topic read watcher/heartbeat
topic read watcher/console_heartbeat

# ============ watcher user (console page) ============
user watcher
# Page publishes telemetry and status to the bridge
topic write watcher/telemetry
topic write watcher/status

# Audio: page publishes PTT/wake-word audio directly to the bridge
topic write watcher/audio
# Heartbeats: page publishes device + console heartbeats (audit 4a, 2026-09-27)
topic write watcher/heartbeat
topic write watcher/console_heartbeat
# Bridge status and ping: page receives status, sends pings
topic readwrite watcher/bridge
# Device commands: page receives from agent only
topic read watcher/command
# Keepalive and jiggler: page publishes config, receives remote state
topic readwrite watcher/keepalive
topic readwrite watcher/jiggle
# Bridge keepalive/jiggle: page reads the bridge's takeover claims and
# remote-drive messages (audit 4b/4c, 2026-09-27)
topic read watcher/keepalive_bridge
topic read watcher/jiggle_bridge
# Muse driving state: page receives only
topic read watcher/muse
# Pause state: bidirectional
topic readwrite watcher/muse_pause
# Command queue: bidirectional
topic readwrite watcher/muse_queue

# ---- Auditor notes (Muse) ----
# 1. RESOLVED 2026-09-27 (audit 4a): watcher/heartbeat and
#    watcher/console_heartbeat now have `topic write` for the watcher
#    user. Previously silently dropped by the broker (default-deny).
# 2. UPDATED 2026-11-07: watcher now has write on watcher/audio
#    (muse already had read). This removes the broker-side blocker to
#    the console routing t:audio messages directly to watcher/audio
#    instead of batching them into watcher/telemetry. The console
#    routing change itself remains separate.
# 3. muse has read-only on watcher/jiggle and watcher/keepalive, plus
#    write on the new watcher/jiggle_bridge + watcher/keepalive_bridge
#    (single-writer splits, audit 4b/4c). Direct bridge writes to the
#    page-owned topics stay forbidden.
# 4. 2026-09-26: an ACL-vs-topics checker guards every publish
#    (topic_acl.py + audit_topics.py). Runtime: all bridge publish paths
#    go through publish_checked() — ungranted topics are BLOCKED locally
#    with a loud ACL-DENY banner. Static: audit_topics.py checks every
#    bridge publish site (AST) + every page mqttPublish site (parsed
#    from watcher-console.html). Run the static audit before shipping
#    any bridge/console patch and after any broker ACL change
#    (re-mirror this file first).
# 5. 2026-11-07: John confirmed the broker was updated, the local
#    mirror (mosquitto-acl-20260925.acl) was synced to this file, and
#    the static audit was re-run against the mirrored broker state.
